Subject: Test the array itself, not defined(@v), in Foomatic::PPD::_tag

Perl 5.22 and later refuse defined() on an array at compile time, so the
module does not load. An empty array is what the test means.

--- a/lib/Foomatic/PPD.pm
+++ b/lib/Foomatic/PPD.pm
@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@
 sub _tag {
     my ($t, @v) = @_;
 
-    return '' if !defined(@v);
+    return '' if !@v;
 
     if (0) {
 	$v =~ s!\&!\&amp\;!g;
